{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lichnerowicz","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-lichnerowicz","kind":"proposition","title":"Categorical Lichnerowicz: $\\Delta_\\nabla^q = \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla^2 + \\tfrac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{Sc}_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-dirac-operator","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hodge-laplacian-relation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-laplacian-expansion","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-hodge-star","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-instanton","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-categorical-reeb-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-categorical-reeb-brings","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-u1-chart-swap"],"cites":["references/lichnerowicz1963","references/woronowicz1989"],"tags":["lichnerowicz","weitzenbock","q-laplacian","categorical-dirac","spin-geometry","self-duality","clifford"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Lichnerowicz.qDirac","text":"categorical-lichnerowicz.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lichnerowicz.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-lichnerowicz\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code> be a categorical connection on an adjoint bundle over the contact affine chart with Reeb derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Hodge star <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla = q^{-1}\\nabla + \\hbar_q \\, \\iota_\\xi \\nabla</code> be the categorical Dirac operator, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\nabla^q</code> the categorical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian. On the categorical-instanton saddle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star_q F_\\nabla = F_\\nabla</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Delta_\\nabla^q  =  \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla^2  +  \\tfrac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{Sc}_q,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sc}_q</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-scalar curvature. On the Bring background, the Reeb generator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi = e_3</code> is parallel, forcing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sc}_q = 0</code> and simplifying the identity to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\nabla^q = \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla^2</code>. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-scalar curvature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Sc}_q = R + O(\\hbar_q)</code> encodes both the classical scalar curvature and the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-anomaly contribution from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 \\neq 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-lichnerowicz.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.16.9"}
